    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d387">

                <pb facs="0401" n="389" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg389"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A Recruiting/209: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Capetown</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Denby</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-17T18:00:00-05:00">April 17, 1941—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. For the Minister. Your 37, April 10, 4 p.m. South African Minister discussed
                    this matter on March 10 with Department<anchor n="10" xml:id="d387-f1"/> which
                    informed him that it has in principle no objection but that matter would have to
                    be considered in connection with national defense needs. Minister was then
                    referred to American Red Cross with which he is understood to be continuing
                    conversations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d387-f1" n="10" xml:id="d387-f1-content">
                <p>Memorandum by the Chief of the Special Division, dated March 10, 1941, not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
